<title>FRANCE: Air France freight at 60 pct in dispute.</title>
<headline>Air France freight at 60 pct in dispute.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France said it should maintain 60 percent of its scheduled full-freighter programme during a two-day period of industrial action by airline staff beginning on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Pilots and crews at several French airlines are protesting over deregulation and what they see as unfair competition in the European air transport industry.</p>
<p>&quot;Of 14 Boeing 747-200F flights scheduled to operate today (Wednesday) and tomorrow (Thursday), we expect to have to cancel six,&quot; an Air France cargo official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Air France said it should maintain one quarter of short-haul passenger flights and two-thirds of long-haul passenger flights during the strike.</p>
